{
    "name": "E2E SurveyMonkey - new survey trigger",
    "description": "Creates a survey, sends the New Survey trigger a survey_created event signed with the secret of the webhook the trigger registered, asserts the emitted survey and deletes it.",
    "notes": {
        "3226f83a-9bc3-43c2-9160-d132dac98b40": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 368,
            "width": 960,
            "height": 304,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Self-provoked trigger\n\n`NewSurvey.start()` registers a real `survey_created` webhook at SurveyMonkey, and `stop()` deletes it. The event itself does not come from SurveyMonkey: on the E2E account (Basic plan, draft app) SurveyMonkey accepts the webhook and checks its URL, but delivers no events (probed 2026-11-18 with `survey_created`, `survey_updated` and `response_completed`).\n\nThe provoke lane therefore lists the webhooks, picks the one named `Appmixer New Survey <trigger id>`, reads its `authorization` secret back from SurveyMonkey and POSTs an event in SurveyMonkey's documented shape to the trigger's own webhook URL (`g_webhookUrl` with the component id replaced). The trigger checks the secret and reads the survey from the API, so the whole receive path runs against the real account.\n\nThe `Condition` drops events of surveys created by anyone else during the run. On an account where SurveyMonkey does deliver events, the real event and the posted one both reach the trigger; the second one fails in the cleanup because the survey is already deleted."
        }
    },
